00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.960
So as you may know, the president has declared a national emergency, which seeks to divert eight billion dollars

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.760
away from areas previously allocated by Congress

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.800
to build a US-Mexico border wall.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.400
This is very important for a lot of reasons.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.680
Let's get into it.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.200
As you've probably heard, the US government just

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.400
reopened after the longest shutdown in his history of 35 days.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.800
Now, why was it shutdown?

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.520
Well quite frankly because Congress couldn't agree on a budget bill that they knew the president would sign.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.240
Under Article 1 of the Constitution

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.600
Congress has the power of the purse, which basically means they have the power to control

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.320
The money of the United States of America.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.320
Now, that's their department. That's their branch of government.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.960
However, they can't pass a budget bill or a law solely on their own.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.360
The balance of powers require that the president sign off on a bill or a budget in order for it to

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.040
Become law. So here's where this really starts to matter.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.320
Well the president signed off on the budget, that budget didn't include.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.680
the eight billion dollars of funding that he wanted to build the US-Mexico border wall.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.720
So what is he to do, if he really wants to make this happen?

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.880
He either has to quit and go on.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.240
Or - if you're on an unorthodox guy - you can invoke your national emergency powers.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:05.200
What is required exactly for a president to be able to declare a national emergency and what is it?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.960
First and foremost, a national emergency is a power that a president can use to

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:13.240
basically, give them extra power in a moment of crisis.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.880
Way back in 1911, Woodrow Wilson was the first one to

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.440
declare a national emergency and after him, presidents really liked it.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.280
They started declaring more of them.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.280
FDR declared a bunch of them.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.760
The problem was, that at no point during these declarations

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.760
did the president cite relevant statutes which gave them the authority to declare an emergency.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.830
They didn't cite the scope or for how long an emergency was supposed to be in effect

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.360
So it started to get into unfettered power territory.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.240
In 1976, Congress passed the National Emergencies Act.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.040
Which limits the authority from which a president can declare an emergency

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.440
To about a hundred and thirty five statutes.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.880
It also requires that if a president is to declare an emergency,

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.640
he must cite one of those statutes as the basis for his power.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.680
On February 15th

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.160
The president declared his construction authority from one of these statutes.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.400
Specifically, 10 USC 2808 a.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.920
I have the statute right here.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.000
I'm gonna read it to you

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.560
with my handy dandy piece of paper.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.920
In the event of a declaration by the president of a national emergency

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.760
that requires the use of the armed forces,

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.760
the Secretary of Defense, may undertake and authorize military construction projects

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.760
not otherwise authorized by law

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.360
which are necessary to support such use of the Armed Forces.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.640
That's what the president is basing his authority off of.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.600
What does that mean?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.560
Well number one, you need the armed forces to be at the border

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.440
in order for this to be even relevant.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.680
Well, that's true, the armed forces are at the border.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.760
Secondarily, the construction aspect of this statute, is supposed to be in support of

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.240
the purpose for which the armed forces are there.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.960
So given what the president is citing for his national emergency authority here.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.160
The only question becomes whether his

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.200
declaration can be seen as legitimate within the bounds of this statute.

